Induct on the elimination stage for support. Initially every nonzero upper-triangular entry is an edge by [F1]. Suppose the inclusion holds at stage $k$ and $S^{k+1}_{ij}
e0$ for $i<j$. If $S^k_{ij}
e0$, its edge is retained by [F2]. Otherwise the correction term is nonzero. Since $\mathbb C$ is a field by [F4], applying [F3] to $(S^k_{iv_k}p_k^{-1})S^k_{v_kj}$ and then to $S^k_{iv_k}p_k^{-1}$ shows that $S^k_{iv_k}
e0$ and $S^k_{v_kj}
e0$. Hermitian symmetry from step 1.1 gives the undirected edges from $i$ to $v_k$ and from $v_k$ to $j$ in the active graph. Hence both vertices are later neighbors of $v_k$, and [F2] inserts $\{i,j\}$. This proves the support inclusion at stage $k+1$.

For each accepted block, $D_r$ is invertible by its pivot test. Direct block multiplication gives [given, F1, algebra]
$$\begin{pmatrix}D_r&B_r^*\\B_r&C_r\end{pmatrix}
=\begin{pmatrix}I&0\\B_rD_r^{-1}&I\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}D_r&0\\0&C_r-B_rD_r^{-1}B_r^*\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}I&D_r^{-1}B_r^*\\0&I\end{pmatrix},$$
with the right-hand side an ordinary matrix product. Thus in exact arithmetic each elimination step is a valid Hermitian congruence and, when all stages finish, their product is $PAP^*=LD_{\rm blk}L^*$.

At each permitted strict-lower position, the recurrence gives $l_{ij}=
u_{ij}/l_{jj}$ and step 2.1 gives $l_{jj}>0$. Hence $
u_{ij}
e0$ implies $l_{ij}
e0$. Under the stated no-cancellation condition every permitted position is nonzero; together with step 4.1 this gives equality of patterns.
